course: dictionary
lesson: 12292
title: Convinced: sure, or talked round
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Convinced» tells you that a person is completely sure something is true. Look at the words around it: «Sam was convinced the shop was open on Sunday, so he walked all the way there.» He was sure, so he acted on it.
explain: Sometimes the belief turns out to be wrong, and that is what makes a story funny. «Mia was convinced the moon was made of cheese, until her teacher showed her the photos.» Convinced means she was sure, even though she was mistaken.
explain: «Convinced» can also mean someone was talked into something. «Dad convinced me to try the spicy soup, and I liked it.» Check the sentence: is somebody being persuaded to change their mind?
explain: Watch for small phrases. «Be convinced that» means be sure that. «Not convinced» means you still have doubts. Read the words after convinced as well as before it.
fact: Convinced means completely sure that something is true.
fact: Convinced is also the past form of convince, which means to make someone believe something or agree to do something.
fact: «Not convinced» means you still have doubts.
fact: A good scientist is convinced only by evidence, meaning clear proof.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «sure» or «talked into» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Tom was convinced it would rain, so he took his umbrella.» What does convinced mean here? | Very cross | Tired and hungry | Lost in the park | *Completely sure
exercise: «Ella convinced her mum to let her stay up for the film.» What did Ella do? | *She made her mum agree | She hid the television | She forgot about the film | She slept early
exercise: «I am not convinced the bus will come on time.» What does «not convinced» mean? | Fast asleep | *Still doubtful | Completely sure | Very happy
test: «The scientist was convinced only by the clear evidence.» Why was she convinced? | Because her friend shouted | *Because the proof was clear | Because she was tired | Because it was her birthday
test: «Jo was convinced the box was full of gold, but it was full of rocks.» What is funny about this? | Jo went straight home | *Jo was sure of something that was wrong | The box was very big | Jo found real gold
exam: Which sentence uses convinced to mean talked someone into something? | «I was convinced the sun had gone out.» | *«Max convinced his brother to share his crisps.» | «The dog was convinced it was a cat.» | «The river was convinced and cold.»
